    "body": "Does this mean DOMParser currently permits forcing arbitrary queued microtasks to be flushed “synchronously” (from the POV of the flush-inducing code) at will? I’d have expected (naively, anyway — I may not be picturing this right) the microtask checkpoint algorithm to be a noop any time user code is already on the execution stack.",
