    "updated_at": "2023-01-04T11:50:27Z",
    "body": "Just wondering, is it possible that there is something \"that delays the load event\" here? If I'm not mistaken, scripting is disabled by lack of a browsing context, so I guess the two first lists of scripts from step 5 and step 7 should always already be empty, but I'm not quite sure about this step 8, though it seems that most requests are also blocked because the Document is not \"fully active\".  \r\n\r\nAsking because this reminds me of https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6230 where it was already spotted that browsers apparently don't really spin the event loop when the condition is already met. I guess the same could be happening here (assuming in your tests you don't have the microtask-checkpoint). Note: I agree that a strict reading of the specs indeed would ask for it to be visited, and incur a microtask-checkpoint, and it also seems true that most of this \"the end\" seems off for these parsers.",
